			<div id="content" class="site-content">
		<div class="ast-container">
				<div data-elementor-type="wp-page" data-elementor-id="260" class="elementor elementor-260" data-elementor-post-type="page">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a29f07da e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent" data-id="a29f07da" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3b563b19 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="3b563b19" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><header class='hero'><div class='bg-mesh'><div class='blob blob1'></div><div class='blob blob2'></div><div class='blob blob3'></div></div><div class='wrap hero-in'><span class='pill'><i></i> Beauty Marketing Agency · Abu Dhabi &amp; Al Ain</span><h1>The beauty marketing agency Abu Dhabi clinics hire to be found <span class='hl'>in Arabic and English.</span></h1><p class='sub'>The capital books differently. Clients search in two languages, clinic ads sit under the Department of Health – Abu Dhabi, and the emirate stretches from Al Reem and Saadiyat to Khalifa City and Al Ain. We plan SEO, Google &amp; Meta Ads and booking around all three.</p><div class='hero-ctas'><a href='/get-a-free-audit/' class='btn btn-grad'>Book My Abu Dhabi Audit</a><a href='#districts' class='btn btn-line'>See How We Plan Each District</a></div><div class='stat-row'><div class='stat-card'><b>4.14M</b><span>Abu Dhabi emirate residents, 2024</span><small>Source: <a href='https://scad.gov.ae/w/abu-dhabi-population-in-2024-grows-7-5-to-reach-4-14m' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>SCAD</a></small></div><div class='stat-card'><b>AR + EN</b><span>Every campaign built in both languages</span></div><div class='stat-card'><b>100%</b><span>Beauty &amp; aesthetics only</span></div></div></div></header></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a3e667e2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="a3e667e2" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section><div class='wrap'><div><span class='kicker'>The Abu Dhabi market, honestly</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Why a Dubai playbook <span class='hl'>under-performs in the capital</span></h2></div><div class='niche' style='margin-top:44px'><div class='prose'><p>Abu Dhabi is an emirate of three regions, not one city. The Statistics Centre – Abu Dhabi counted 4,135,985 residents in 2024: roughly 68% in the Abu Dhabi region, 24% in the Al Ain region and 8% in Al Dhafra. A clinic on Al Maryah Island and a ladies' salon in Al Ain are both “in Abu Dhabi”, but they serve different people, different commutes and different search habits. So we scope campaigns by region first, then by district.</p><h3>Two languages, two sets of keywords</h3><p>Arabic is the official language of the UAE, and in the capital a large part of beauty search happens in it. A client looking for a henna artist, bridal makeup or a dermatologist may type in Arabic, in English, or in transliterated “Arabizi”. Translated English ads miss a lot of that. We write Arabic copy natively, build separate Arabic keyword sets for Google Ads, and make sure your Google Business Profile, website and booking flow work in both languages. If your salon serves mostly Arabic-speaking clients, our <a href='/arabic-beauty-salon/'>Arabic beauty salon marketing</a> service goes deeper on this.</p><h3>A younger, male-heavy population changes the mix</h3><p>SCAD reports a median age of 33, with 54% of residents aged 25–44, and a population that is about 67% male. Most agencies only target women. Here, men's grooming and barbering is a large market of its own. Al Ain City Municipality counted 1,190 beauty centres in Al Ain in 2024, and 791 of them were men's centres. We plan separate creative and audiences for men's and ladies' services, not one mixed campaign.</p><h3>Visitors and event weekends</h3><p>The Department of Culture and Tourism reported 5.8 million hotel guests across the emirate in 2024. Yas Island draws big event crowds too, including the Formula 1 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix at Yas Marina Circuit, set for 3–6 December 2026. For salons and clinics near Yas, Saadiyat and the Corniche hotels, we schedule ad budgets and “near me” campaigns around those dates instead of spending the same amount every week.</p></div><div class='niche-card'><h3>Abu Dhabi, at a glance</h3><ul><li><b>4.14M</b> residents in the emirate, up 7.5% on 2023</li><li><b>~1M</b> in the Al Ain region: a market of its own</li><li><b>33</b> median age, and 54% are 25–44</li><li><b>1,190</b> beauty centres in Al Ain alone (791 men's, 399 women's)</li><li><b>5.8M</b> hotel guests in 2024</li></ul><small class='src'>Sources: <a href='https://scad.gov.ae/w/abu-dhabi-population-in-2024-grows-7-5-to-reach-4-14m' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>SCAD, Population 2024</a> · <a href='https://dmt.gov.ae/en/aam/Media-Centre/News/Al-Ain-City-Municipality-organizes-the-Health-and-Beauty-Forum' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Al Ain City Municipality, Jul 2024</a> · <a href='https://en.aletihad.ae/news/business/4579524/abu-dhabi-hotel-sector-booms-with-5-8-million-guests-in-2024' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>DCT 2024 Hotel Performance Report via Aletihad</a></small></div></div></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7f5fc123 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="7f5fc123" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section style='background:#FBFAFE'><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker'>Who regulates what in Abu Dhabi</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Clinics answer to the DoH. <span class='hl'>Salons answer to the municipality.</span></h2><p class='sub'>Clinics and salons in Abu Dhabi report to different authorities, so a marketing plan has to start with knowing which rules apply to you. This is how we read it. It is not legal advice, so confirm your own case with the authority.</p></div><div class='reg-grid'><div class='reg'><span class='tag'>Clinics, medspas, dermatology</span><h3>Department of Health – Abu Dhabi (DoH)</h3><p>The DoH is the emirate's healthcare regulator. It licenses healthcare facilities and the professionals who work in them, and it also regulates advertising of health products and services in Abu Dhabi and issues the permits for it. In Dubai, the DHA does that job. Approval for an Abu Dhabi clinic ad comes from the DoH, and promotions for medical products also need prior approval from the federal Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP).</p><p>What this means for your marketing:</p><ul><li>Treat every ad, boosted post and promo for a medical or aesthetic service as health advertising. Plan time for DoH approval before launch. TAMM lists DoH services to log and re-log a health advertisement.</li><li>Keep claims something you can prove. Leave out “guaranteed results” and “no side effects” style wording.</li><li>Make sure the treatments you promote match your facility licence and your practitioners' DoH licences.</li></ul><small>Sources: <a href='https://www.ibanet.org/document?id=Healthcare-Survey-Responses-2024-United-Arab-Emirates' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>IBA Healthcare Survey 2024 – UAE</a> · <a href='https://www.tamimi.com/law-update-articles/termination-of-general-clinic-licences-in-abu-dhabi-implementation-of-new-primary-healthcare-centre-licence/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Al Tamimi – DoH facility licensing</a> · <a href='https://www.tamm.abudhabi/en/life-events/business/Manage-your-Business/Advertisement/RequestforHealthAdvertisement' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>TAMM – Request to Log a Health Advertisement</a></small></div><div class='reg'><span class='tag'>Salons, barbers, beauty centres</span><h3>Abu Dhabi City Municipality &amp; Al Ain City Municipality (DMT)</h3><p>Non-medical salons and beauty centres are inspected for public health and hygiene by the municipalities under the Department of Municipalities and Transport (DMT). In April 2024, Abu Dhabi City Municipality's Public Health Department ran more than 100 inspection visits on beauty centres, ladies' salons and barbershops before Eid Al-Fitr. A September 2025 campaign cited Law No. (2) of 2012 and its executive regulations. Al Ain City Municipality runs its own inspections and industry forums.</p><p>What this means for your marketing:</p><ul><li>Hygiene and sterilisation are what inspectors check, and clients notice them too. Show them in your content.</li><li>If you advertise laser, injectables or any medical-grade treatment, check first whether it falls under DoH rules.</li><li>Expect inspection campaigns before Eid, when salons are busiest. Book your peak-season ads around them.</li></ul><small>Sources: <a href='https://www.dmt.gov.ae/en/adm/Media-Centre/News/03Apr2024' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>DMT, 3 Apr 2024</a> · <a href='https://www.dmt.gov.ae/en/adm/Media-Centre/News/17Sep2025' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>DMT, 17 Sep 2025</a> · <a href='https://dmt.gov.ae/en/aam/Media-Centre/News/Al-Ain-City-Municipality-organizes-the-Health-and-Beauty-Forum' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Al Ain City Municipality, Jul 2024</a></small></div></div><p class='reg-note'>Our <a href='/clinic-marketing-uae-guide/'>guide to compliant clinic marketing in the UAE</a> covers claims, before-and-after content and platform policies. If you run a clinic, see how we work with <a href='/aesthetic-clinics/'>aesthetic clinics</a> and <a href='/dermatology-clinics/'>dermatology practices</a>.</p></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ea8cefed elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="ea8cefed" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section style='background:#fff'><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker'>Services, set up for the capital</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>What we run for Abu Dhabi salons &amp; clinics, <span class='hl'>and how it changes here</span></h2><p class='sub'>These are the same services we offer everywhere. In Abu Dhabi, each one is set up for Arabic-speaking clients, the DoH rules and the distances between the city, Yas and Al Ain.</p></div><div class='svc-grid'><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/seo-for-beauty-salons-clinics/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M4 19V5M4 19h16'/><path d='M8 15l3.5-4 3 2.5L19 8'/></svg></span><h3>Local SEO, Abu Dhabi</h3><p>Pages and Google Business Profiles in English and Arabic, so you rank for “صالون تجميل” as well as “beauty salon” in your area.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/clinic-google-maps-ranking/'>Read: Why clinics drop out of Google Maps →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/google-ads-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><circle cx='11' cy='11' r='7'/><path d='M21 21l-4.3-4.3'/></svg></span><h3>Google Ads, Abu Dhabi</h3><p>Separate Arabic and English ad groups, plus location targeting that keeps Al Ain spend apart from Abu Dhabi city spend.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/clinic-google-ads-keywords/'>Read: Which clinic keywords are worth bidding on →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/instagram-facebook-ads-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M3 11l16-6-4 14-5-4-3 3v-5z'/></svg></span><h3>Instagram &amp; Facebook Ads, Abu Dhabi</h3><p>Ads written natively in Arabic and English, with separate men's grooming and ladies' audiences. Clinic ads go through DoH approval before launch.</p></a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/ai-appointment-booking-bot/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H4l2-3a8 8 0 1 1 15-5z'/></svg></span><h3>Bilingual AI Booking Assistant</h3><p>Answers WhatsApp and web enquiries in Arabic or English, so a message sent after hours still ends in a confirmed booking.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-whatsapp-booking-leak/'>Read: Where WhatsApp bookings leak →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/websites-landing-pages-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><rect x='3' y='4' width='18' height='13' rx='2'/><path d='M8 21h8M12 17v4'/></svg></span><h3>Websites with a Real Arabic Version</h3><p>Proper right-to-left Arabic layouts, not a translate widget. Treatment pages are written so your clinic can stand behind every claim.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-website-conversion-fixes/'>Read: 7 fixes that make a site book →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/social-media-management-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M12 3l1.8 4.6L18 9l-4.2 1.4L12 15l-1.8-4.6L6 9l4.2-1.4z'/><path d='M18 15l.9 2.1L21 18l-2.1.9L18 21l-.9-2.1L15 18l2.1-.9z'/></svg></span><h3>Social Media for Abu Dhabi Brands</h3><p>Content calendars planned around Ramadan, Eid, National Day and Yas event weekends, in the tone your clients use.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-content-ideas-30-days/'>Read: 30 days of salon content ideas →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/ecommerce-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M6 7h12l1 13H5z'/><path d='M9 10V6a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v4'/></svg></span><h3>Online Shop &amp; Gift Cards</h3><p>Sell Eid gift vouchers, bridal packages and retail skincare online, with delivery to clients across the emirate, including Al Ain.</p></a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/reviews-reputation/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M12 3l2.7 5.5 6 .9-4.3 4.2 1 6-5.4-2.8L6.6 19.6l1-6L3.3 9.4l6-.9z'/></svg></span><h3>Reviews in Both Languages</h3><p>Review requests and replies in Arabic and English, because a reply in the client's own language reads as respect.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-bad-review-response-templates/'>Read: How to answer a 1-star review →</a></div><div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/services/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><rect x='3' y='3' width='18' height='18' rx='5'/><circle cx='12' cy='12' r='4'/><circle cx='17.2' cy='6.8' r='1'/></svg></span><h3>Capital Growth Plan</h3><p>Combine SEO, ads and booking into one plan scoped to your region, whether that is Abu Dhabi island, the mainland suburbs or Al Ain.</p></a></div></div></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c6fe71df elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="c6fe71df" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd' id='gwd-districts-auh-v2'><section class='district-sec' id='districts'><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker' style='color:var(--lime)'>Interactive · Area planner</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px;color:#fff'>From the island to Al Ain, <span style='color:var(--lime)'>one emirate, six briefs</span></h2><p class='sub' style='color:#A7A2B6;margin:14px auto 0'>Pick an area to see how we would plan for it. These are our planning notes, not survey data. Your free audit checks them against your real competitors and search data.</p></div><div class='district-tabs'><button class='dtab on' data-d='reem'>Al Reem Island</button><button class='dtab' data-d='khalidiya'>Khalidiya &amp; Al Zahiyah</button><button class='dtab' data-d='bateen'>Al Bateen</button><button class='dtab' data-d='yas'>Yas &amp; Saadiyat</button><button class='dtab' data-d='khalifa'>Khalifa City &amp; Al Raha</button><button class='dtab' data-d='alain'>Al Ain</button></div><div class='dpanel on' id='auh2-reem'><div><h3>Al Reem Island</h3><p>A tower-living island just off the downtown grid, with many residents who moved there for work. Most people find a salon or clinic within a short drive, so being visible on the map in your own cluster of towers matters more than a citywide campaign.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Apartment towers</span><span>English-first, Arabic close behind</span><span>Short-radius search</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Maps + Instagram</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Radius we'd test</span><b>The island itself</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>Many new openings</b></div></div></div><div class='dpanel' id='auh2-khalidiya'><div><h3>Khalidiya &amp; Al Zahiyah</h3><p>Old, central neighbourhoods with long-running salons and loyal clients. Many of those clients book through word of mouth and WhatsApp. Arabic review replies and a complete, up-to-date Google profile usually matter more here than a flashy ad.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Established central areas</span><span>Repeat clients</span><span>WhatsApp booking culture</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Reviews + Local SEO</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Language mix</span><b>Arabic &amp; English</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>Parking-led search</b></div></div></div><div class='dpanel' id='auh2-bateen'><div><h3>Al Bateen</h3><p>A quieter, villa-heavy and well-established part of the island. Clients here value discretion and trust. For a dermatology or aesthetic clinic, that means a careful, claim-safe website and appointment-only messaging. Discount-led ads tend to work against you.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Villas &amp; residences</span><span>Discretion valued</span><span>Premium clinics</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Search + website</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Tone</span><b>Understated, bilingual</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>DoH ad approval</b></div></div></div><div class='dpanel' id='auh2-yas'><div><h3>Yas &amp; Saadiyat Islands</h3><p>These are Abu Dhabi's leisure and culture islands: Yas has Yas Marina Circuit, Yas Mall and Etihad Arena, and Saadiyat has the Louvre Abu Dhabi and its beach resorts. Residents book like locals, but on event weekends demand rises from hotel guests. We raise budgets around those dates rather than spending flat all year.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Residents + hotel guests</span><span>Event-driven peaks</span><span>Mobile “near me” search</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Google Ads + Maps</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Timing</span><b>Event calendar</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>Hotel spas compete</b></div></div></div><div class='dpanel' id='auh2-khalifa'><div><h3>Khalifa City &amp; Al Raha</h3><p>Mainland family suburbs between the airport and the islands. Many residents would rather not drive onto the island for a blow-dry or a facial. A salon that ranks well locally on the mainland can win them over. Home-service and ladies-only offers are worth testing here.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Family villas</span><span>Avoid the island commute</span><span>Ladies-only demand</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Local SEO</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Language mix</span><b>Strong Arabic share</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>Wide catchment</b></div></div></div><div class='dpanel' id='auh2-alain'><div><h3>Al Ain</h3><p>The emirate's second city, with around a million people in the Al Ain region according to SCAD. It has its own municipality and is a long drive from the capital. Al Ain City Municipality counted 1,190 beauty centres in 2024, and 791 of them serve men. Al Ain needs its own campaigns, its own Google profile and Arabic-first creative. It should not be a corner of an Abu Dhabi city budget.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Separate city, separate budget</span><span>Arabic-first</span><span>Large men's grooming market</span></div></div><div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Where we start (Glowth view)</span><b>Arabic search + Maps</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Regulator for salons</span><b>Al Ain City Municipality</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Watch-out</span><b>Don't target the whole emirate</b></div></div></div><p class='dnote'>Al Ain figures: <a href='https://dmt.gov.ae/en/aam/Media-Centre/News/Al-Ain-City-Municipality-organizes-the-Health-and-Beauty-Forum' target='_blank' rel='noopener' style='color:#C6F432;text-decoration:underline'>Al Ain City Municipality, Jul 2024</a> · <a href='https://scad.gov.ae/w/abu-dhabi-population-in-2024-grows-7-5-to-reach-4-14m' target='_blank' rel='noopener' style='color:#C6F432;text-decoration:underline'>SCAD 2024</a>. All other notes are Glowth's planning view.</p></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-18d071ca elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="18d071ca" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section style='background:#FBFAFE'><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker'>Local SEO, in two languages</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Show up on the map <span class='hl'>whichever language she searches in</span></h2><p class='sub'>Many Abu Dhabi clients search Google Maps in Arabic. If your Google Business Profile only has English categories, services and replies, you are much less visible to them. We build the profile, services list and review replies in both languages.</p></div><div class='maps'><div class='mhead'><span>Search: “عيادة جلدية خليفة سيتي” (dermatology clinic, Khalifa City)</span><em>Illustrative example</em></div><div class='mrow you2'><span class='pin'>★</span><div><b>Your Clinic · عيادتك</b><small>Arabic + English profile · Replies in both languages</small></div><span class='tag2'>GOAL: TOP 3</span></div><div class='mrow'><span class='pin'>B</span><div><b>Competitor clinic</b><small>English-only profile</small></div></div><div class='mrow'><span class='pin'>C</span><div><b>Another clinic</b><small>Few recent reviews</small></div></div></div><p class='mfoot'>This is a mock-up, not real ranking data. See <a href='/clinic-google-maps-ranking/'>why clinics fall out of the Google Maps results</a> for what actually moves rankings.</p></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ed7cd95f elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="ed7cd95f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker'>Side by side</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>A capital-focused beauty agency vs. <span class='hl'>a Dubai-first generalist</span></h2></div><div class='compare'><div class='cmp-row cmp-head'><div></div><div class='glow'>Glowth in Abu Dhabi</div><div>Typical generalist</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Arabic ad copy &amp; keywords</div><div class='yes'>Written natively, separate ad groups</div><div class='no'>Translated from English</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Clinic ad approvals</div><div class='yes'>Plans time for DoH approval before launch</div><div class='no'>Uses Dubai DHA habits</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Al Ain</div><div class='yes'>Treated as its own market</div><div class='no'>Lumped into “Abu Dhabi”</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Men's grooming</div><div class='yes'>Separate audiences &amp; creative</div><div class='no'>Women-only targeting</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Event weekends (Yas, holidays)</div><div class='yes'>Budgets moved to match</div><div class='no'>Same spend every week</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Sector focus</div><div class='yes'>Beauty &amp; aesthetics only</div><div class='no'>Any industry</div></div><div class='cmp-row'><div>Contract</div><div class='yes'>Monthly rolling</div><div class='no'>Often 6–12 months</div></div></div></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8279ebbf elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="8279ebbf" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					<div class='gwd'><section style='background:#FBFAFE'><div class='wrap'><div class='center'><span class='kicker'>FAQs</span><h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Questions Abu Dhabi owners ask us</h2></div><div class='faq'><details open><summary>Does my Abu Dhabi clinic need approval before running ads?</summary><p>For medical and aesthetic services, generally yes. The Department of Health – Abu Dhabi regulates advertising of health products and services in the emirate and issues the permits. Medical product promotions also need prior MOHAP approval. We plan approval time into every launch. For your exact case, check the current DoH requirements on TAMM.</p></details><details><summary>Should my salon's ads and Google profile be in Arabic, English, or both?</summary><p>For most Abu Dhabi businesses, both. Arabic and English searchers use different words, so a translated ad usually performs worse than one written natively. We run separate Arabic and English ad groups and keep your Google Business Profile, website and review replies bilingual.</p></details><details><summary>Can one campaign cover Abu Dhabi city and Al Ain?</summary><p>We don't recommend it. Al Ain is a separate city of around a million people (SCAD, 2024), with its own municipality and a long drive from the capital. A shared campaign usually spends money in the area where you have no branch. If you have branches in both, each gets its own location targeting, Google profile and budget.</p></details><details><summary>Who inspects beauty salons and barbershops in Abu Dhabi?</summary><p>The municipalities under the Department of Municipalities and Transport: Abu Dhabi City Municipality and Al Ain City Municipality, through their public health teams. They run regular hygiene inspection campaigns, often before Eid. Medical-grade treatments are a different matter and fall under the DoH.</p></details><details><summary>Is men's grooming worth a separate marketing budget here?</summary><p>Often, yes. SCAD reports Abu Dhabi's population is about 67% male. In Al Ain, the municipality counted 791 men's beauty centres out of 1,190 in 2024. If you serve men, they need their own creative, offers and audiences, not a footnote in a ladies' campaign.</p></details></div></div></section></div>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d861fd00 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="d861fd00" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
